.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_BARRIER 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_barrier_new ,
.Nm dtfl_barrier_wait ,
.Nm dtfl_barrier_free
.Nd reusable all-workers barrier
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_barrier *
.Fn dtfl_barrier_new "dtfl_worker *w"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_barrier_wait "dtfl_barrier *b"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_barrier_free "dtfl_barrier *b"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A barrier is a reusable rendezvous across all workers.
.Fn dtfl_barrier_new
builds a small dataflow with one input and a probe on it.
Every worker must create its barriers in the same order.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_barrier_wait
advances this worker one round and steps the worker until the probe
reports that round reached, which happens only once every worker has
advanced to it.
Waiting does not block dataflow execution: other dataflows on the worker
keep running during the wait.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_barrier_free
drops the barrier and its dataflow.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_barrier *b = dtfl_barrier_new(worker);
for (int round = 0; round < iterations; round++) {
	do_phase(round);
	dtfl_barrier_wait(b);	/* all workers reach here together */
}
dtfl_barrier_free(b);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
These functions do not return error codes.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_execute 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_sequencer_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Vt Barrier
of
.Pa synchronization/barrier.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A barrier belongs to the worker thread that created it.
Every worker creates and waits on its own barrier; the rendezvous
across workers happens through the dataflow's progress tracking, not
through shared memory.
